# policy-verifier.toolchain-pin — legacy pin mirror (issue #41, REQ-D95).
#
# COMPATIBILITY MIRROR ONLY: the verifier derives its expected pin from
# the repo-root rust-toolchain.toml `channel` (fail-closed when absent).
# This file exists because scripts/verify-rigs.sh V9 passes it explicitly
# via --pin-file; its content MUST equal the rust-toolchain.toml channel
# (enforced by tests/test_policy_verifier.py). Source of truth is
# rust-toolchain.toml — on a toolchain bump, change the channel there
# AND the snapshot `pin:` line AND this mirror together.
